<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Rental Agreement — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Transfer of Property Act 1882, Karnataka Rent Act 1999, Registration Act 1908 (Sec 17)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>₹100 to ₹200 Non-Judicial e-Stamp Paper (for lease up to 11 months in Karnataka)</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Optional for agreements up to 11 months; Compulsory under Section 17 Registration Act if tenancy exceeds 11 months</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Notarization before Notary Public recommended along with two adult witnesses</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Jurisdiction of Civil Court / Rent Controller where the leased property is situated</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>3 years from cause of action (for recovery of unpaid rent / security deposit)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Aadhaar Card / PAN Card of Landlord (Lessor); Aadhaar Card / PAN Card of Tenant (Lessee); Original Title Deed / Khata Extract of Property (Verification of Ownership); Latest Electricity / Water Bill & Property Tax Paid Receipt; Two Passport Size Photographs of each party</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">RENTAL AGREEMENT</div>
<div class="draft-body">RENTAL AND LEASE AGREEMENT

This Rental Agreement is made and executed on this _____ day of _______________, 2026 at ________________________, Karnataka, by and between:

LESSOR (LANDLORD):
Name: __________________________________________________
S/o, D/o, W/o: __________________________________________
Aadhaar No.: ____________________________________________
Permanent Address: ______________________________________
________________________________________________________
(Hereinafter referred to as the "LESSOR", which expression shall unless repugnant to the context mean and include his/her legal heirs, executors, administrators, and assigns of the FIRST PART);

AND

LESSEE (TENANT):
Name: __________________________________________________
S/o, D/o, W/o: __________________________________________
Aadhaar No.: ____________________________________________
Permanent Address: ______________________________________
________________________________________________________
(Hereinafter referred to as the "LESSEE", which expression shall unless repugnant to the context mean and include his/her legal heirs, executors, administrators, and assigns of the SECOND PART).

WHEREAS the Lessor is the absolute owner in lawful physical possession of the residential/commercial premises bearing Door/Flat No. __________________, situated at ______________________________________________________________________, Karnataka (hereinafter referred to as the "SCHEDULE PREMISES").

AND WHEREAS the Lessee has approached the Lessor to take the Schedule Premises on rent for residential/commercial purpose and the Lessor has agreed to let out the same on the terms and conditions agreed hereunder:

NOW THIS AGREEMENT WITNESSETH AS UNDER:

1. TENANCY PERIOD:
The tenancy shall be for a fixed term of 11 (Eleven) calendar months commencing from ___/___/2026 and expiring on ___/___/2027. The agreement may be renewed mutually on fresh terms and conditions with written consent.

2. MONTHLY RENT:
The Lessee agrees to pay a monthly rent of Rs. ____________/- (Rupees _________________________________________ only), payable on or before the 5th day of every succeeding English calendar month via Bank Transfer / UPI / Cheque.
Account Details: Bank: __________________, A/c No: ______________________, IFSC: __________________.

3. INTEREST-FREE REFUNDABLE SECURITY DEPOSIT:
The Lessee has paid a sum of Rs. ____________/- (Rupees _________________________________________ only) as interest-free refundable security deposit to the Lessor. The receipt whereof the Lessor hereby acknowledges. The said deposit shall be refunded to the Lessee upon handing over vacant physical possession of the premises, subject to deduction of unpaid rent, utility bills, or painting/damages charges.

4. UTILITY CHARGES & MAINTENANCE:
The Lessee shall promptly pay the monthly electricity consumption charges, water charges, and society maintenance charges as per actual meter readings and bills issued by BESCOM/BWSSB or Residents Welfare Association.

5. USE OF PREMISES:
The Lessee shall use the Schedule Premises strictly and exclusively for residential purposes and shall not conduct any commercial, hazardous, unlawful, or immoral activities therein, nor cause nuisance to neighbors.

6. REPAIRS & ALTERATIONS:
The Lessee shall keep the interior in good, tenantable condition. Minor day-to-day repairs (tap washers, fuse, bulbs) shall be borne by the Lessee. Major structural repairs shall be the responsibility of the Lessor. The Lessee shall not make any structural additions or alterations without prior written permission of the Lessor.

7. SUB-LETTING & ASSIGNMENT:
The Lessee shall not sub-let, assign, transfer, or part with the physical possession of the premises or any part thereof to any third party under any circumstances.

8. INSPECTION:
The Lessor or authorized representative shall have the right to inspect the premises at reasonable daytime hours upon giving 24 hours prior notice to the Lessee.

9. NOTICE PERIOD & TERMINATION:
Either party may terminate this agreement prior to the expiry of the 11-month term by giving 1 (One) month advance written notice or paying one month's rent in lieu thereof. If the Lessee defaults on rent payment for consecutive 2 months, the Lessor reserves the right to terminate the tenancy and seek eviction immediately.

10. PAINTING & VACATION:
At the time of vacating the premises, the Lessee shall restore the premises in the same clean and painted condition as received, or the Lessor shall deduct one month's rent towards painting charges from the security deposit.

11. JURISDICTION:
In the event of any dispute arising out of this agreement, the Civil Courts at ________________________, Karnataka shall have exclusive jurisdiction.

SCHEDULE OF THE PROPERTY:
All that piece and parcel of residential premises bearing Flat/Door No. __________, located at _____________________________________________________________________, comprising of ___ Bedrooms, Hall, Kitchen, Balconies, fitted with electric and sanitary fixtures.
East by: ____________________________________
West by: ____________________________________
North by: ___________________________________
South by: ___________________________________

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the LESSOR and the LESSEE have set their hands and signed this Rental Agreement on the day, month, and year first above written in the presence of the following witnesses:

LESSOR (LANDLORD):                               LESSEE (TENANT):
Signature: __________________________            Signature: __________________________
Name: _______________________________            Name: _______________________________

WITNESSES:
1. Signature: _______________________            2. Signature: _______________________
   Name: ____________________________               Name: ____________________________
   Address: _________________________               Address: _________________________
   Aadhaar: _________________________               Aadhaar: _________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>